target: internal/record/record.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestLoadsStructuralRulesThatNothingElseAsserts'
expect: a_run_known_only_by_a_nudge_exists_and_has_no_cycles
why:    runlog.load does `runs.setdefault(rid, {})` BEFORE it looks at the phase, so a run known only by a nudge row exists and has no cycles. Skipping unmodelled phases before the run is created makes it vanish instead, which survived the whole suite: no fixture carried a nudge row, though the real store has 17. It matters because review-stats' abandonment accounting keys on a plan with no finish, so a disappearing run changes a number rather than erroring.
